  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "For entrepreneur Cassidy Lobaugh, Grand Lake in Oklahoma first meant summers at her grandparents’ fishing cabin. Vernon and Wanda Lively’s gatherings brought the family together for card games, fish fries and nights on a screened porch. She later joined the purchase of nearby land and the development of The Sunset Chapel on Paradise Bluffs.\n\nThe site’s evening light shaped the venue. Lobaugh and her family positioned the chapel towards the western horizon, using the cross already raised on the property to help set out its foundation. She proposed anniversary photography sessions and preferential bookings for families returning to celebrate other occasions.",
    "html": "<p>For entrepreneur Cassidy Lobaugh, Grand Lake in Oklahoma first meant summers at her grandparents’ fishing cabin. Vernon and Wanda Lively’s gatherings brought the family together for card games, fish fries and nights on a screened porch. She later joined the purchase of nearby land and the development of The Sunset Chapel on Paradise Bluffs.</p>\r\n<p>The site’s evening light shaped the venue. Lobaugh and her family positioned the chapel towards the western horizon, using the cross already raised on the property to help set out its foundation. She proposed anniversary photography sessions and preferential bookings for families returning to celebrate other occasions.</p>\r\n",
